00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:34,110
the answer, and some of you here may remember. No, I don't think there are many around here

64
00:09:34,110 --> 00:10:04,070
That in the early 50s, we concluded that modern management, or as good many people concluded, modern management, especially in the large corporation, was the first governance in the world that could really succeed on the basis of performance without having a boss, without being accountable.

65
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:12,170
the shareholders had become so dispersed it wasn't AT&T alone that had more than a million

66
00:10:12,170 --> 00:10:18,880
shareholders not one of them owning more than a couple of hundred shares same was true of PM

67
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:31,390
and of all the biggest that they had ceased to count when so a hard-working competent management

68
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:38,010
could work on the performance of the business or the institution

69
00:10:38,010 --> 00:10:46,810
and do it by balancing and in the process balance the claims and interests

70
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:51,030
of a number of, we call them constituents today, we call them stakeholders,

